3. Find the First Order of Every Customer(Infosysloo que)
SELECT *
FROM (
    SELECT
        order_id, customer_id, customer_name,order_date,
        quantity * unit_price AS order_amount,
        ROW_NUMBER() OVER(
            PARTITION BY customer_id
            ORDER BY order_date
        ) AS rn
    FROM orders
) t
WHERE rn = 1;

Why the subquery?: Ikkada first Calculate row number -> Then filter rn = 1 -- The window function is calculated before the outer filter

4. Find the Latest Order of Every Customer (Same idea, reverse the sorting):
SELECT *
FROM (
    SELECT
        order_id,customer_id, customer_name, order_date,
        quantity * unit_price AS order_amount,
        ROW_NUMBER() OVER(
            PARTITION BY customer_id
            ORDER BY order_date DESC
        ) AS rn
    FROM orders
) t
WHERE rn = 1;

5. RANK(): Rank orders by amount
SELECT
    order_id,customer_name,
    quantity * unit_price AS order_amount,
    RANK() OVER(
        ORDER BY quantity * unit_price DESC
    ) AS amount_rank
FROM orders; -- gap vachindaa?

